{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "LiquidLeakingEmissions",
    "description": "Steps L1, L9 and O1-O3 of the process-evap-leaks chain: the emission itself, the inspection-and-maintenance blend, and the MOVESOutput row. Ports docs/evap-leaks.md §2.5, joins K15-K22, and crates/moves-calculators/src/calculators/liquid_leaking_calculator.rs:606 (L1) and :859-1020 (L9 and the output row).\n\nONE PRODUCT AND ONE DIVISION.\n\n    emissionQuant = weightedMeanBaseRate x sourceHours x opModeFraction / noOfRealDays\n\nThe grouping is `((rate x hours) x fraction) / days`, in that order, because that is the order the reference multiplies in and binary64 is not associative; the emitted values agree with MOVESOutput to 1.0e-08 at the newest cohort and 1.3e-06 at the oldest, which is the snapshot's six-significant-figure column storage and not accumulated error (docs/evap-leaks.md §7.1).\n\nWHY `/ noOfRealDays` IS THERE AT ALL. A7 divides the month's VMT by `noOfDays / 7` so that SHO covers one average WEEK -- that is, `noOfRealDays` days of the day type. L9 divides that back out to one day. Applying the factor in both places, or in neither, is a factor of 2 on the weekend rows and 5 on the weekday rows; baseratecalculator/mod.rs:1536-1542 records the rates-first analogue. The weekday/weekend ratio of a single cohort is 3.80618 rather than 2.5 for that reason (docs/evap-leaks.md §6.4), and no factor in that product is 1.\n\nTHE TWO SOAK MODES ARE PRESENT AND CARRY EXACTLY ZERO. Rows 2 and 3 are the hot- and cold-soak modes of the 1980 gasoline cohort, with real non-zero rates of 0.430904708 and 0.22403231499999998 g/h and an opModeFraction of 0 -- because components/evap_operating_mode_distribution.esm COMPUTES that zero from `fractionOfOperating = 1` rather than assuming it. O1 sums the three modes, so a document that dropped the fractions would emit 4.692285338 x hours instead of 4.037348315 x hours: a 16.2% over-emit with the right key set, the right pollutant and no NaN anywhere.\n\nTHE I/M BLEND IS INERT ON THIS FIXTURE AND IS EXERCISED ANYWAY. `imcoverage` and `imfactor` are both EMPTY in the snapshot, so L1 produces no cell and L9's `UPDATE` leaves every row untouched -- `pollutantprocessassoc` nevertheless marks polProcessID 113 `isAffectedByEvapIM = 'Y'`, so this is an absent PROGRAM and not a structural exclusion, and a county with an evap I/M program would exercise it. The `.esm` spells the absence as `IMAdjustFract = 0`, for which lib/adjustments.esm's `im_blend` is the identity. That template was authored in Phase 1 as \"the onroad inspection/maintenance blend PLAN.md §3 names; it is not exercised by the NONROAD slice\", and this is the first chain that reaches it -- so it is exercised here by a PROBE row, the technique docs/esm-conventions.md §16.4 established after finding F19 removed the parameter-override one.\n\nROWS 7 AND 14 ARE THAT PROBE AND THEIR NUMBERS ARE NOT MOVESOutput'S. They carry model year 1990, gasoline, with a round base rate of 1 g/h, an I/M rate of 0.5 g/h and an `imcoverage`-derived `IMAdjustFract` of 0.3 -- none of which is in the snapshot. Model year 1990 IS a real cohort of the fixture; what is invented is its rate and its I/M coverage, so the two output rows for it, 0.46902999999999995 g and 1.7852040000000002 g, are hand arithmetic from this file's own inputs and are NOT the reference's values for that cohort. Every other row in this file reaches a cell of MOVESOutput. The probe uses real `sourceHours` for age 30, 1.1036 h and 10.5012 h, so only the rate and the coverage are constructed.\n\nWHAT THIS COMPONENT EMITS AND WHAT IT DOES NOT. `out_*` here is the load-bearing subset of the 25-column MOVESOutput schema: the three varying keys, the quantity, the computed SCC, the pollutant and process the pollutant-process splits into, the link's road type, and one of the nine columns that must be ABSENT. The full schema belongs to the fixture, which is where a missing column is a comparison failure rather than a review point. `out_regClassID` is `lib/identifiers.esm`'s `null_output_column` -- 0/0, a NaN -- because emitting 0 would claim regulatory class zero, and because the comparator reads NaN, NULL and empty as the same thing. On this fixture the regClassID group-by is a no-op, since `sourcebin` carries only class 20; the column must still be absent.\n\nData: the six weighted mean base rates are components/evap_weighted_base_rate.esm's own output, verified equal to it; `sh_sourceHours` and `omd_opModeFraction` are the two upstream relations the assembly joins instead. Everything else is the snapshot's (docs/evap-leaks.md §6.0-§6.3).",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "moves",
      "onroad",
      "evaporative",
      "emission",
      "output",
      "component"
    ]
  },
  "enums": {
    "pollutant": {
      "TotalGaseousHydrocarbons": 1
    },
    "process": {
      "EvapFuelLeaks": 13
    },
    "source_type": {
      "PassengerCar": 21
    },
    "fuel_type": {
      "Gasoline": 1,
      "EthanolE85": 5
    },
    "road_type": {
      "UrbanRestrictedAccess": 4
    },
    "hour": {
      "SevenAM": 7
    },
    "day_type": {
      "Weekend": 2,
      "Weekday": 5
    },
    "operating_mode": {
      "HotSoaking": 150,
      "ColdSoaking": 151,
      "Operating": 300
    }
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "leak_emission_rows": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 14
    },
    "leak_source_hour_rows": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 8
    },
    "leak_op_mode_rows": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 6
    },
    "leak_hour_day_rows": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 2
    },
    "leak_day_rows": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 2
    },
    "im_coverage_rows": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 1
    },
    "leak_pol_process_rows": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 1
    },
    "leak_link_rows": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 1
    },
    "leak_output_rows": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 10
    }
  },
  "coordinates": {
    "leak_output_model_year": {
      "source": "out_modelYearID",
      "standard_name": "vehicle_model_year"
    },
    "leak_output_scc": {
      "source": "out_SCC",
      "standard_name": "source_classification_code"
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "LiquidLeakingEmissions": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "../lib/adjustments.esm",
          "only": [
            "im_blend"
          ]
        },
        {
          "ref": "../lib/identifiers.esm",
          "only": [
            "pol_process_id",
            "pollutant_id_of",
            "process_id_of",
            "null_output_column",
            "output_column_is_absent"
          ]
        },
        {
          "ref": "../lib/onroad_activity.esm",
          "only": [
            "onroad_scc"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "tolerance": {
        "rel": 1e-12
      },
      "variables": {
        "runYearID": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 2020.0,
          "description": "runspecyear.yearID. A scalar: it is an operand of the subtraction that builds the derived age key, not a join key itself (docs/esm-conventions.md §16.1)."
        },
        "runPolProcessID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_pol_process_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The run's pollutant-process, 100 x 1 + 13 = 113, built by `pol_process_id`. K17's join key, and a one-row relation for the reason §16.1 gives."
        },
        "ppa_pollutantID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_pol_process_rows"
          ],
          "description": "pollutantprocessassoc[113].pollutantID = 1, unpacked from the pollutant-process by `pollutant_id_of` rather than written, so that the packing at the input and the unpacking at the output cannot disagree (lib/identifiers.esm)."
        },
        "ppa_processID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_pol_process_rows"
          ],
          "description": "pollutantprocessassoc[113].processID = 13, likewise by `process_id_of`."
        },
        "link_roadTypeID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_link_rows"
          ],
          "description": "link[2616104].roadTypeID = 4, Urban Restricted Access. An ON-network road type, which is what makes SourceHours = SHO at A10 and therefore what makes this whole slice independent of finding F12 (docs/evap-leaks.md §0.3). It is also the road-type slot of the output SCC."
        },
        "hd_hourDayID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_hour_day_rows"
          ],
          "description": "hourday.hourDayID = hourID x 10 + dayID for hour 7: 72 and 75."
        },
        "hd_dayID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_hour_day_rows"
          ],
          "description": "hourday.dayID: 2 (weekend), 5 (weekday). K18 carries it to the emission row and O1 groups on it."
        },
        "hd_hourID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_hour_day_rows"
          ],
          "description": "hourday.hourID = 7 on both rows. `hourofanyday[7].hourname` is \"Hour beginning at 6:00 AM\"; the enum is named for the identifier, not the wall clock."
        },
        "dow_dayID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_day_rows"
          ],
          "description": "dayofanyweek.dayID, K19's right-hand side."
        },
        "dow_noOfRealDays": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_day_rows"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "dayofanyweek.noOfRealDays: 2 real days in a weekend, 5 in a week of weekdays. L9's DIVISOR, and the factor A7 multiplied in."
        },
        "sh_hourDayID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_source_hour_rows"
          ],
          "description": "sourcehours.hourDayID. Rows are hour-day-major, four ages each."
        },
        "sh_ageID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_source_hour_rows"
          ],
          "description": "sourcehours.ageID: 0, 18, 30 and 40 -- the ages the five cohorts of this file reach at 2020."
        },
        "sh_sourceHours": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_source_hour_rows"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "sourcehours.sourceHours, in hours: the zone's vehicle-hours in one hour of one day type, summed over that day type's real days in an average week. Equal to `sho.SHO` row for row because the link is on-network (A10). The snapshot's own six-significant-figure values, docs/evap-leaks.md §6.0."
        },
        "omd_hourDayID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_op_mode_rows"
          ],
          "description": "opmodedistribution.hourDayID. Rows are hour-day-major, three operating modes each."
        },
        "omd_opModeID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_op_mode_rows"
          ],
          "description": "opmodedistribution.opModeID: 150, 151, 300 within each hour-day block. Carried as data because a product relation can make only one of its two key columns contiguous (docs/esm-conventions.md §16.2)."
        },
        "omd_opModeFraction": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_op_mode_rows"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "components/evap_operating_mode_distribution.esm's output, carried here as a column so this file tests standalone; the assembly joins the two instead. {150: 0, 151: 0, 300: 1} on both hour-days, and every one of those three numbers is COMPUTED there rather than assumed."
        },
        "im_processID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "im_coverage_rows"
          ],
          "description": "IMCoverageMergedUngrouped.processID. A PROBE row: `imcoverage` and `imfactor` are both empty in this snapshot, so L1 produces nothing and this relation would be empty. See the description."
        },
        "im_pollutantID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "im_coverage_rows"
          ],
          "description": "IMCoverageMergedUngrouped.pollutantID, 1."
        },
        "im_modelYearID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "im_coverage_rows"
          ],
          "description": "IMCoverageMergedUngrouped.modelYearID, 1990 -- L1 disaggregates each IMCoverage record across the individual model years its [begModelYearID, endModelYearID] range covers, so this relation is model-year-per-row and the range predicate (K20's `filter`) lives upstream of it."
        },
        "im_fuelTypeID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "im_coverage_rows"
          ],
          "description": "IMCoverageMergedUngrouped.fuelTypeID, 1."
        },
        "im_sourceTypeID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "im_coverage_rows"
          ],
          "description": "IMCoverageMergedUngrouped.sourceTypeID, 21."
        },
        "im_imAdjustFract": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "im_coverage_rows"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "SUM of `IMFactor x complianceFactor x 0.01` over the programs covering this key. 0.3 on the probe row, which blends the I/M rate in at weight 0.3 and the non-I/M rate at 0.7."
        },
        "emis_hourDayID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_emission_rows"
          ],
          "description": "L9's hour-day key. Rows 1-7 are hourDayID 72 and rows 8-14 are 75, so this column is built from the `hour` and `day_type` enums in two contiguous blocks."
        },
        "emis_fuelTypeID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_emission_rows"
          ],
          "description": "L9's fuel key: gasoline except on rows 5 and 12, which are the E85 cohort of docs/evap-leaks.md §6.3."
        },
        "emis_modelYearID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_emission_rows"
          ],
          "description": "L9's model-year key: 1980 three times (one per operating mode), then 2002 twice (gasoline and E85), 2020, and the 1990 I/M probe."
        },
        "emis_opModeID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_emission_rows"
          ],
          "description": "L9's operating-mode key. 300 everywhere except rows 2, 3, 9 and 10, which are the hot- and cold-soak modes of the 1980 gasoline cohort."
        },
        "emis_sourceTypeID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_emission_rows"
          ],
          "description": "L9's source-type key, 21 throughout. K21 joins on it."
        },
        "emis_effectiveAgeID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_emission_rows"
          ],
          "description": "`runYearID - modelYearID`: K15's join key into `sourceHours`. components/evap_weighted_base_rate.esm computes the same subtraction for K12 and carries it on the rate relation; the assembly takes it from there rather than repeating it, because moves.rs writes it at :767 and :935 and a port that wrote it twice has two chances to disagree with itself."
        },
        "emis_weightedMeanBaseRate": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_emission_rows"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "L8's output, in grams of THC per hour, from components/evap_weighted_base_rate.esm: 4.037348315, 0.430904708, 0.22403231499999998, 1.353566677, 0.000192737741, 0.12496779679999999 and the probe's 1. `g h-1` is not a registry unit so the unit is named here and not declared."
        },
        "emis_weightedMeanBaseRateIM": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_emission_rows"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "L8's second measure. Zero everywhere except the probe rows, whose 0.5 g/h is what makes the blend observable."
        },
        "emis_sourceHours": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_emission_rows"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "K15: `sourceHours` brought to the row on (hourDayID, ageID), with the year, month, link and source type from the iteration context. One clause, two pairs here; the reference's is six pairs, four of which are run scope in this component."
        },
        "emis_opModeFraction": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_emission_rows"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "K16: the operating-mode fraction brought to the row on (hourDayID, opModeID). 1 on the mode-300 rows and 0 on the four soak rows."
        },
        "emis_dayID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_emission_rows"
          ],
          "description": "K18: `hourday.dayID`. The output row carries the day and the hour separately, not the packed hourDayID."
        },
        "emis_noOfRealDays": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_emission_rows"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "K18 and K19 as one contraction: hourDayID to dayID to noOfRealDays. Two clauses over two relations, composing by conjunction."
        },
        "emis_imAdjustFract": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_emission_rows"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "K21: the I/M adjustment fraction, on five key pairs. Zero on every row but the two probes -- and a zero here is the SQL's \"no matching row, keep the value unchanged\", for which `im_blend` is the identity. `IMCoverageMergedUngrouped` carries at most one cell per key (it is L1's GROUP BY result), which is what makes folding the UPDATE into this join equivalent."
        },
        "emis_emissionQuant": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_emission_rows"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "L9: `((weightedMeanBaseRate x sourceHours) x opModeFraction) / noOfRealDays`, in grams. The grouping is the reference's; binary64 is not associative and the alternative groupings differ in the last bits."
        },
        "emis_emissionQuantIM": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_emission_rows"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "The same product over `weightedMeanBaseRateIM`, in grams. L9's second working column."
        },
        "emis_blendedQuant": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_emission_rows"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "L9's trailing UPDATE: `im_blend(emissionQuantIM, IMAdjustFract, emissionQuant)`, which is `GREATEST(qIM x f + q x (1 - f), 0)`. Equal to `emis_emissionQuant` on the twelve rows with no I/M cell."
        },
        "out_dayID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_output_rows"
          ],
          "description": "MOVESOutput.dayID. Rows 1-5 are the weekend and rows 6-10 the weekday, so the column is built from the `day_type` enums in two contiguous blocks."
        },
        "out_fuelTypeID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_output_rows"
          ],
          "description": "MOVESOutput.fuelTypeID, carried as data because gasoline occurs in disjoint runs."
        },
        "out_modelYearID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_output_rows"
          ],
          "description": "MOVESOutput.modelYearID: 1980, 2002, 2002, 2020 and the 1990 probe, twice."
        },
        "out_polProcessID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_output_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The pollutant-process, 113, built by `pol_process_id`. It is not a MOVESOutput column; it is the join key that splits into the two that are."
        },
        "out_pollutantID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_output_rows"
          ],
          "description": "MOVESOutput.pollutantID = 1, from K17."
        },
        "out_processID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_output_rows"
          ],
          "description": "MOVESOutput.processID = 13, from K17. It is also the last two digits of the SCC."
        },
        "out_roadTypeID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_output_rows"
          ],
          "description": "MOVESOutput.roadTypeID = 4, from the link. `tolerance.toml` lists it among the columns the comparator ignores, because two implementations legitimately disagree on it -- but the SCC's road-type slot is computed from it, and that is compared."
        },
        "out_SCC": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_output_rows"
          ],
          "description": "O2: `22e8 + fuelTypeID x 1e6 + sourceTypeID x 1e4 + roadTypeID x 1e2 + processID` (engine.rs:1450-1477), by lib/onroad_activity.esm's `onroad_scc`. 2201210413 for gasoline and 2205210413 for E85. It is COMPUTED, not looked up: the `scc` table's 14,976 rows agree with the formula and are read by nothing in this chain."
        },
        "out_regClassID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_output_rows"
          ],
          "description": "MOVESOutput.regClassID, which this run leaves NULL on all 128 rows: `null_output_column` is 0/0, a NaN, and the comparator reads NaN, NULL and empty as the same thing. Emitting 0 would claim regulatory class zero. One of nine absent columns; the other eight are the fixture's business."
        },
        "out_emissionQuant": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_output_rows"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "O1: the sum of `emis_blendedQuant` over the operating modes, in grams of THC. The 1980 gasoline rows sum three modes of which two contribute exactly zero; every other row is one mode. Eight of the ten values are cells of the snapshot's MOVESOutput and two are the labelled I/M probe."
        },
        "out_regClassIsAbsent": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_output_rows"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "O3's testable half: `output_column_is_absent(out_regClassID)`, which is 1 where the column is NaN and 0 for any real value. It exists because absence is the one property of a NULL output column that cannot be pinned directly -- `expected` is a JSON number so NaN cannot be written down, and every tolerance form is a magnitude comparison that a NaN actual fails (measured: `actual=NaN expected=0` reports FAIL, the right verdict and the wrong polarity). This column turns that into an assertion with a non-zero expected value."
        },
        "out_emissionQuantIsAbsent": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "leak_output_rows"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "The NEGATIVE control for the indicator above -- the same template applied to a column that is PRESENT, so it reads 0 on every row. Without it, an indicator that returned 1 unconditionally would satisfy the absence test, which is the failure mode gates/equijoin_undriven_control.esm exists for one level up. docs/esm-conventions.md 12 puts it as: assert both arms of a branch."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": "runPolProcessID",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "makearray",
            "args": [],
            "regions": [
              [
                [
                  1,
                  1
                ]
              ]
            ],
            "values": [
              {
                "op": "apply_expression_template",
                "args": [],
                "name": "pol_process_id",
                "bindings": {
                  "pollutant_id": {
                    "op": "enum",
                    "args": [
                      "pollutant",
                      "TotalGaseousHydrocarbons"
                    ]
                  },
                  "process_id": {
                    "op": "enum",
                    "args": [
                      "process",
                      "EvapFuelLeaks"
                    ]
                  }
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "ppa_pollutantID",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "pollutant_id_of",
            "bindings": {
              "pol_process_id": "runPolProcessID"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "ppa_processID",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "process_id_of",
            "bindings": {
              "pol_process_id": "runPolProcessID"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "link_roadTypeID",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "makearray",
            "args": [],
            "regions": [
              [
                [
                  1,
                  1
                ]
              ]
            ],
            "values": [
              {
                "op": "enum",
                "args": [
                  "road_type",
                  "UrbanRestrictedAccess"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "hd_hourDayID",
          "rhs": {
